# The simulator makefile's output directory (makefile: BIN = BIN/, and every
# target invokes MKDIRBIN, so a clone without it builds fine). Five binaries
# were committed into it by accident; a build product in the tree is a second
# source of truth for something the makefile already produces, and it leaves
# the tree permanently dirty after any build, which is how a real uncommitted
# change went unnoticed through an end-of-session clean-tree check.
BIN/

# Precompiled headers. Upstream shipped sim_console.h.gch and it was removed
# in "Remove the checked-in precompiled header": on a fresh clone it is newer
# than its source, so gcc silently prefers it and a patched header has no
# effect at all.
*.gch

# The simulator's debug trace files. Every one of these is opened
# `fopen(name, "w")` (or the port's `genode_trc_open`) when a `d debug*`
# command turns tracing on, and nothing ever reads one back, so each is a run
# product written into whatever directory the simulator was started in --
# which, for the native build, is this tree. Four of them were tracked
# (`trace.log`, `trace_3271.log`, `trace_A.log` empty, `trace_S.log` holding a
# 16/10/2026 scanner header), so any run with tracing on left the tree dirty.
# That is the same defect as the committed `BIN/` above and it cost the same
# thing: an end-of-session "the tree is clean" check that cannot answer, with
# a real uncommitted change sitting right through it. The pattern covers all
# seven names the source opens -- the 3274, DLSw and Trunk ones were simply
# never committed yet.
trace*.log
